<?xml version="1.0" ?>

<!-- shifting-freeSurface.xml
Shifting is a method to improve the quality of the particle distribution 
and reduce numerical instabilities through the introduction of a small 
corrective displacement in the particle motion equation.

This corrective displacement is computed from local measures of disorder,
typically based on kernel gradients, and applied on top of the physical velocity field.

The shifting vector is evaluated using a the SPH approximation given in

Sun, P. N., et al. "A consistent approach to particle shifting in the δ-Plus-SPH model." 
Computer Methods in Applied Mechanics and Engineering 348 (2019): 912-934.

This the correction for particles close to the free surface.
This preset works together with the free-surface detector algorithm, see detector.xml. 

Remember that after including this preset, a new control parameter for each particle set 
should be imposed, the shifting factor (typically Uref = Ma cs), which scales the intensity
of the corrective displacement.
-->

<sphInput>
    <Variables>
        <Variable name="kappa" type="int*" length="N" />
	<Variable name="region" type="int*" length="N" />
    </Variables>
    <Tools>
	<Tool action="insert" after="Sort" type="set" name="cfd Reinit kappa" in="kappa" value="1"/>
	<Tool action="insert" after="Sort" type="set" name="cfd Reinit region" in="region" value="0"/>
	<Tool action="insert" after="cfd du" type="kernel" name="free surface kappa" entry_point="threshold" path="../../../Scripts/cfd/shifting/shifting-freesurface.cl"/>
	<Tool name="free surface region" action="insert" after="free surface kappa" type="kernel" entry_point="region" path="../../../Scripts/cfd/shifting/shifting-freesurface.cl"/>
	<Tool action="insert" after="free surface region" type="kernel" name="free surface correction" entry_point="entry" path="../../../Scripts/cfd/shifting/shifting-freesurface.cl"/>
    </Tools>
</sphInput>
